--   A genuinely compiled dispatcher suffices if the source strategy is correct and its actual runs have dimension-polynomial state widths and round counts.
-- statement:
--   A genuinely compiled dispatcher suffices if the source strategy is correct and its
--   actual runs have dimension-polynomial state widths and round counts. The single machine,
--   input encoding, output bit and full adaptive transcript are all those of the reference.
--   Polynomial parameters and code are fixed before the public or hidden inputs.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.PriceGame.Control.campaignProgram_correct`.
